d{gap:4px 10px;margin:6px 0}.physics-footnote{margin:4px 0 0}}\n</style>\n<style>\n:is(#editor-controls,#models-transform) input[type=number]{box-sizing:border-box;background:#26384d;color:#fff;border:1px solid #4b6078;border-radius:5px;padding:6px;font:inherit}:is(#editor-controls,#models-transform) input:disabled{opacity:.5}#pickup-editor button:disabled{cursor:default;opacity:.5}#editor-status{color:#91dce4}#editor-error:empty{display:none}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id="stage" aria-busy="false"><canvas id="canvas" tabindex="0" aria-label="Track view. Camera controls are described in the viewer panel."></canvas></main>\n<aside aria-label="Track viewer controls">\n<h1>Rollcage, Stage II &amp; Firebugs track viewer</h1>\n<p class="note">Select <strong>ROLLCAGE.IMG</strong> and <strong>ROLLCAGE.IDX</strong> for Rollcage or Stage II, or a <strong>Firebugs PS1 disc ZIP</strong> containing its CUE and data BIN.</p>\n<div class="row"><label for="game">Game</label><select id="game"><option value="auto">Automatic</option><option value="rollcage">Rollcage</option><option value="stage2">Rollcage Stage II</option><option value="firebugs">Firebugs</option></select></div>\n<div id="pc-files">\n<p class="note">Both files are usually located in:<br><strong>Rollcage:</strong><br><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Psygnosis\\Rollcage\\IDXData</code><br><strong>Rollcage Stage II:</strong><br><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Psygnosis\\Rollcage Stage II\\IDXData</code></p>\n<p class="note">You can paste the folder path for your game into the Browse dialog.</p>\n<label class="file" for="image">Rollcage.img<input id="image" type="file" accept=".img"></label>\n<label class="file" for="index">Rollcage.idx<input id="index" type="file" accept=".idx"></label>\n</div>\n<div id="disc-files"><label class="file" for="disc">Firebugs disc ZIP<input id="disc" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip"></label></div>\n<p class="note">Files are read locally and stay on your computer. Select another source to switch games. Disc loading can take a moment while the data BIN is decompressed; audio tracks are skipped.</p>\n<p id="game-info" class="note"></p>\n<div class="row"><label for="track">Track</label><select id="track" disabled aria-label="Track"></select><button id="reload" type="button">Load / retry</button></div>\n<p id="status" role="status">Select both Rollcage.img and Rollcage.idx, or a Firebugs disc ZIP.</p>\n<p id="error" role="alert"></p><p id="counts" class="note"></p>\n<p id="scene-scope" class="note"></p>\n<button id="download" type="button" disabled>Download track</button>\n<p class="note">Want a single model? Open the <a href="object-viewer.html">3D Object Viewer</a>.</p>\n<p class="note">Saves the static track and ordinary objects as a ZIP with OBJ, materials and PNG textures. The racing cars and path overlays stay in the viewer. Unzip it, then import scene.obj into Blender.</p>\n<fieldset style="border:1px solid #344457;border-radius:5px"><legend>Racing test</legend>\n<p id="racing-warning" class="note" style="color:#ffd48a"><strong>Super experimental.</strong> Driving, collisions and lap timing may be inaccurate.</p>\n<div class="racing-actions"><button id="practice-start" type="button" disabled>Start</button><button id="practice-step" type="button" disabled>Step frame</button><button id="practice-recover" type="button" disabled>Test recovery</button><button id="practice-reset" type="button" disabled>Reset race</button></div>\n<div class="row"><label for="practice-ai-count">AI cars</label><input id="practice-ai-count" type="range" min="1" max="6" step="1" value="3" disabled aria-describedby="practice-performance-note"><output id="practice-ai-count-value" for="practice-ai-count">3</output></div>\n<p id="practice-performance-note" class="note" style="color:#ffd48a">Performance warning: the racing simulation runs in JavaScript. More AI cars can lower FPS. Reduce the count if the viewer feels slow. Changing the count restarts the race.</p>\n<div class="row"><label for="practice-car">Car to follow</label><select id="practice-car" disabled></select></div>\n<div class="racing-options"><label><input id="practice-follow" type="checkbox" checked disabled><span id="practice-follow-label">Follow car 1</span></label><label><input id="practice-telemetry" type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-controls="physics-hud">Telemetry</label></div>\n<div class="racing-options"><label><input id="practice-weapons" type="checkbox" checked disabled>Weapons &amp; pickups (experimental)</label></div>\n<p class="note">Changing this option restarts the race. Gold dots mark original pickup locations. AI cars collect and use items; boxes appear and respawn as they race. Audio, weapon trails and some effects are not yet shown.</p>\n<p id="practice-inventory" class="note" style="font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums"></p>\n<p id="practice-roster" class="note"></p>\n<p id="practice-readout" class="note" style="font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums"></p>\n<p id="practice-note" class="note">Available on verified Rollcage tracks, except LEV16 and LEV17.</p><p id="practice-error" class="note" role="alert" style="color:#ffb4ac"></p>\n<details id="practice-progress" class="racing-progress"><summary>Physics progress</summary><p class="note">Racing test now has physical cameras and animated terrain, including LEV8's moving terrain points. Surface acceleration uses the recovered decay and limits.</p><p class="note">Original-game checks now match one complete recorded six-car update, including AI, physics, attachment movement, recovery checks, drive feedback, wheel and animation updates, cameras, weather/world effects, and the final return and clock increments. This check uses recorded external clock and runtime-library results. Other checks cover selected car-to-car, car-wall and camera-border collisions, force responses and controlled respawn placement. Separate instruction checks now cover the clock calculations and step scheduling. Continuous race parity, active co`... 2192333 more characters,
